# Purpose

This document defines every user journey, interaction flow, navigation path,
decision tree, and state transition within MuscleX.

Every screen must belong to one or more user flows.

Every feature must support at least one complete user journey.

No screen may exist in isolation.

---

# UX Philosophy

Users should never ask:

"Where do I go next?"

Every screen must naturally guide users toward the next meaningful action.

The system should minimize thinking and maximize momentum.

---

# Global UX Rules

Every flow must:

✓ Start with a clear entry point

✓ Have a logical progression

✓ Handle loading

✓ Handle offline

✓ Handle errors

✓ Handle cancellations

✓ Handle interruptions

✓ Preserve user progress

✓ End with success feedback

✓ Offer a next recommended action

---

# Global Entry Points

Users can enter the app from:

• Splash Screen

• Push Notification

• Widget

• Deep Link

• QR Code

• AI Assistant

• Search

• Home Dashboard

• External Link

• Gym ERP

• Smart Watch

• Voice Command (Future)

---

# Global Exit Points

Users may leave by:

• Completing a task

• Closing the app

• Backgrounding the app

• Navigating elsewhere

• Sharing content

• Logging out

• Session timeout

• Network interruption

